dsh: reasoning:
Now I know the exact format needed for a review to be counted by the controller scan:

- File in `reviews/*.json`
- `verdict` ∈ accept|revise|reject|inconclusive
- `reviewer` or `actor` = my id (must be distinct from others)
- `counts_as_full_schema_verdict` != False (so omit or true)
- An explicit pin in one of: top-level `artifact_sha256`, `reviewed_sha256`, `sha256`, `cited_sha256`, or nested under `target`/`artifact` dict as `sha256`/`artifact_sha256`/`reviewed_sha256`
- `target_id`/`target`/`target_subnode` string that maps via TARGET_ALIASES to F0/F1/F2a/F2b/L0/L1. Note "F2a" maps to "F2a" (TARGET_ALIASES.get("F2a", ...) → "F2a" since key "F2A" only uppercase... wait `TARGET_ALIASES.get(t, TARGET_ALIASES.get(t.upper(), t))`: for t="F2a", first get("F2a") → not found (key is "F2A"), then get("F2A") → "F2a". Good. For t="F2b" → get("F2b") not found → get("F2B") → "F2b". Good.
